    "media:imagetext": "FOR YOUR SAFETY. Know how to move\nB-747\nout of this airplane fast. There is fire-danger\nany time a landing is other than normal—partic-\nularly when the airplane structure is damaged.\nBelow is a floor plan of the plane you are in. Familiarize yourself with the location of\nthe exits. Note particularly the exits nearest you. Study how they are opened and also\nthe protective position you should assume during an emergency landing. When leav-\ning, do not take coats, purses or baggage with you. Move to the exits immediately.\nA WORD ABOUT YOUR SEAT BELT-Rough air (turbulence) at high altitudes,\nalthough infrequent, can be severe. When seat belt sign is lighted in-flight, please\ncomply with the sign to prevent possible injury. Experienced air travelers usually\nleave their seat belts fastened all the time and pull them up snug when the seat belt\nsign is lighted.\nHOW TO OPEN EXITS\nCA 325\n8-72\nPRINTED IN U.S.A.\nRotate door handle up and\nover. Door moves slightly\ninward and then is auto-\nmatically powered outward\nto a fully open position.\nEscape slide automatically\ndrops and begins inflating\nwhile door is opening.\nUNITED\nThe slide is fully inflated\nand ready for use in a few\nseconds.\nDOUBLE•\nLANE\nSLIDES\nOVERWING\nRAMP AND\n3-LANE\nSLIDES\nJump onto the slide in a sitting position\nusing the closest of the two slide lanes.\nDo not sit down in the doorway. Do not\ntry to slow yourself; special pads at the\nbottom will reduce your speed. Move away\nfrom the bottom of the slide quickly.\nOver-wing door is equipped with inflat-\nable ramp and slide. They inflate auto-\nmatically when the dooris opened. Pro-\nceed along ramp and jump onto slide as\nshown.\n0000\n- JUMF\nONTO\nSLIDE\nHERE\n0000000000\n0000000\nPROCEED\nJUMr\n• ONTO SLIDE\nHERE\nDECELARATION\nDOUBLE-\nLANE\nSLIDES\nDECELERATION PADS\nRUN TO→\nCLEAR AREA\nTO\nAREA",
